From 5b84eecfa1e1b31a9556ecced582239c436e7d62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:12:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(a11y): keep all page content inside landmark regions

Resolves the axe "region" failure reported by the accessibility audit
("Check all visible page content is within defined landmark regions"):

- Design-concept strip (.concept): <div> -> <section aria-label="Design
  concept notice">; decorative dot/separator hidden from AT.
- Homepage utility bar (.utility): <div> -> <nav aria-label="Quick links">.
- Skip link moved from the homepage into the root layout as the first
  element in <body>, so axe recognises it as a skip link and every page
  (not just the homepage) gets one.
- Admin login/dashboard <main> get id="main" so the skip link resolves.

Styling is class-based, so there is no visual change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QzvQx2tHFdthQptX3xTRe5
